  AND NO ARM OF THIS EXPERIMENT REACHES 'CEILING BINDING AT THE PRODUCTION TILE' ON THIS CARD, AT ANY BLOCK_SIZE_N. Over 56 power-of-two tiles up to 2048x1024, 17 clear the ridge of 155.93 Op/B at alpha 0.558 and the smallest accumulator among them is 65536 registers, against a per-block file of 65536. So no tile a thread block can hold is capable of reaching a compute roof here, C4 fails for every control that can be built, and the best verdict any pairing can reach is 'TILE-DEPENDENT GAP, CEILING UNLOCATED'. The two limits very nearly coincide, which is the finding: the register file runs out exactly where the arithmetic intensity would have become enough.
